Dump the predicates the science branches on (validation gate 0).

GLOMAP-mode does not diverge by precision drift. It diverges by flipped
predicates: about ten sites compare a computed float against a threshold and
then select a different closed form. A flip there gives an O(1) difference
between two individually correct float64 implementations, and no trajectory
tolerance can attribute it -- the run simply lands somewhere else. Dumping the
predicates themselves turns "the answer moved" into "this comparison went the
other way, at this substep, in this mode".

Instrumented sites:

  ukca_solvecoagnucl_v  a per-element code naming WHICH of the five closed
                        forms ran, plus the SQD*DTZ > 50 clamp and whether
                        TAN's argument crossed pi/2
  ukca_coagwithnucl     mask1 (both blocks), mask1a, mask2/mask4 for all three
                        mode-pair loops, and the reset loop's MDCPNEW < 0 with
                        mask1 before and after -- the in-place narrowing across
                        ICP that a broadcast port would silently get wrong
  ukca_conden           mask1, mask2 (both definitions), mask3/mask3i/mask4i,
                        and the DELGC_COND > GC guard argued unreachable in
                        UP-4, so the argument becomes an observation
  ukca_remode           nmodemax_merge, the merge trigger, and the FRAC_N 0.5
                        and FRAC_M 0.001 clamps that sit on an erf output
  ukca_calc_drydiam     the ND > NUM_EPS mask and the undersize reset
  ukca_calcnucrate      L1/L2, the Vehkamaki guard, and the three J > 1e-3
                        gates that switch nucleation fully on or fully off
  ukca_binapara         NTOT < 4 with T < 195.15, which replaces the computed
                        rate with a flat 1e5

Substep context comes from ukca_aero_step, the only routine that knows (imts,
izts); leaf routines emit under it. That is why the module keeps context in
SAVEd state rather than taking it as an argument -- ukca_solvecoagnucl_v, which
owns the most valuable predicate in the file, cannot see the counters at all.

Instrumentation only. Every hunk touching src/ukca/ is an INSERTION and reads
only variables that are already live at that point; the build script rejects
any patch that removes a line from a UKCA file. Verified by running the
instrumented binary with and without branch_file set and against an
uninstrumented build: all three trajectories are byte-identical.

Controlled by branch_file in &box_run; empty means not written.

